ess you put all the  pieces together but it makes sense that  the time especially in the early 20s  there weren't a great number of  commercial districts from which they  could choose to shoot and so Hollywood  Boulevard and cahuenga it was close to  their studios and so it was only natural  they would they would go there if they  needed a simple shot of someone walking  you know by a shop window or something  one other thing that's really quaint if  you study what's going on  the background of these films you can  see people in the background you know  they're very respectfully standing and  waiting but in in some of the early  Chaplin films when he's coming in and  out of a storefront you can see the  reflection of people in the windows you  can see people down the street and so  there was a there's always been a great  fascination in watching people shoot  films but even from the very beginning  and I think it's really quaint because  nowadays they would use CGI to erase the  people or have police chase them away  but you know there are people's great  grandparents who are unintentionally in  the background of some of these classic  films  you
 

